      ":question/id": "ff74e3a4-5e8d-5f9a-9158-600c6b1b8fc9",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 3 & 35 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 85\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 3 & 35 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 85\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{35}{2} \\\\ 3 & -2 & 85\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{35}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{13}{2} & \\frac{65}{2}\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{13}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{35}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
