      ":question/id": "d15e5eaf-7e82-5bfa-acd8-9743e6b5b2f4",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 40\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 40\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 40\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 65\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{65}{16}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
