      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -6 & -45 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -30\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -6 & -45 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -30\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -\\frac{45}{2} \\\\ 1 & -2 & -30\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -\\frac{45}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{15}{2}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-\\frac{45}{2} \\\\ y &=-\\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-\\frac{15}{2}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-3\\left(-\\frac{15}{2}\\right)=-\\frac{45}{2}\\,\\Rightarrow\\,x=-\\frac{45}{2}-\\frac{45}{2}=-45.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-45$ and $y=-\\frac{15}{2}.$",
